        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-04T16:33:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this guaranteed to succeed regardless of what profile is passed in? For example, if I were to do:\n\n    mContext.createContextAsUser(UserHandle.of(-5725082))\n\nwould that succeed? Or would it throw? I suppose that since we\u0027re on a binder thread, even if it does throw, the exception will simply be sent back to the caller.\n\nBut given that we keep this UserHandle around and pass it on to the rest of the code (on the handler thread, where we can\u0027t usefully throw any more), it seems like we should validate is somehow. Is there an isValid() method? If not, perhaps we can perform some simplistic validation ourselves like checking that it\u0027s non-negative and \"not too large\"?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9053,
        "startChar": 40,
        "endLine": 9053,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "bc3580809fe36a5e46dedd658463410254021691",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e61db270_61aa3564",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 9053,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-05T13:24:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I\u0027m reading the code correctly, this will throw IllegalStateException(\"Own package not found : \" + getPackageName())\n\nI couldn\u0027t find any way at all in UserHandle or UserManager to validate a UserHandle.\n\nAs for negative, UserHandle.CURRENT is supported and is user -2. I thought a little bit about it and see no real use case for it in this API, but also no strong reason to disallow that particular usage. However, I can find no way to resolve this (the context created here has a getUser() method, but it will happily return the passed one, so -2), which would be necessary to set the correct UID rules.\n\nSo I decided to :\n- Test explicitly for user ID \u003c 0 and reject\n- Catch ISE and translate it into a more appropriate exception for this use case.\nPlease let me know what you think.",
      "parentUuid": "7a2b2fa5_a56e5523",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9053,
        "startChar": 40,
        "endLine": 9053,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "bc3580809fe36a5e46dedd658463410254021691",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
